*** firestore.rules — Aides + class-only discussion creation ***

1) Replace classTeacher() with:

function classTeacher(groupId) {
 return isGroupMember(groupId)
  && get(
    /databases/$(database)/documents/groups/$(groupId)/members/$(request.auth.uid)
     ).data.role in [
       "owner",
       "admin",
       "moderator"
     ];
}

This makes the existing `moderator` storage role the classroom Aide role
for assignment create/update/delete and teacher-visible progress.

2) Replace canModerateForum() with:

function canModerateForum(groupId) {
  return isGroupOwner(groupId)
   || isGroupAdmin(groupId)
   || isGroupModerator(groupId);
}

The role hierarchy is now:
- owner: Primary Teacher / group owner
- admin: Teacher / group admin
- moderator: Aide / group moderator
- member: Student / group member

3) In canDiscipline(), replace the moderator branch:

    (
       get(
         /databases/$(database)/documents/groups/$(groupId)
       ).data.type != "class"
       && isGroupModerator(groupId)
       && moderationTargetRole(groupId, targetUserId) == "member"
    )

with:

    (
       isGroupModerator(groupId)
       && moderationTargetRole(groupId, targetUserId) == "member"
    )

4) Make the same replacement in canDisciplineStoredRole():

  (
     isGroupModerator(groupId)
     && targetRole == "member"
  )

This allows Aides to moderate Students, but not Teachers/Aides.

5) In /groups/{groupId}/forumPosts/{postId}, REPLACE the create rule:

    allow create:
     if platformWriteAllowed()
     && isGroupMember(groupId)
     ...

with:

    allow create:
     if platformWriteAllowed()
     && isGroupMember(groupId)
     && (
       get(
         /databases/$(database)/documents/groups/$(groupId)
       ).data.type != "class"
       || classTeacher(groupId)
     )
     && request.resource.data.userId == request.auth.uid
     && request.resource.data.groupId == groupId
     && request.resource.data.title is string
     && request.resource.data.title.size() >= 2
     && request.resource.data.title.size() <= 200
     && request.resource.data.body is string
     && request.resource.data.body.size() > 0
     && request.resource.data.body.size() <= 10000
     && request.resource.data.pinned == false
     && request.resource.data.locked == false;

Result:
- Ordinary groups: any active member may start a topic, unchanged.
- Classes: only Primary Teacher / Teacher / Aide may start a topic.
- Students may still reply.

6) In moderationReports read access, replace the class-excluding moderator
branch with direct isGroupModerator(groupId):

     if isGroupOwner(groupId)
     || isGroupAdmin(groupId)
     || isGroupModerator(groupId);

Do the same for moderationActions read/create access.

This lets Aides see and act on class moderation reports against Students.

7) In bans read access, replace the class-excluding moderator branch with:

       || isGroupModerator(groupId)

Aide ban creation remains controlled by canDiscipline(), which only permits
them to act against Students.

8) In the nested /members delete rule, replace the comment and moderator
branch so moderators can remove members in a class too.

Replace:

         (
              get(
                /databases/$(database)/documents/groups/$(groupId)
              ).data.type != "class"
              && isGroupModerator(groupId)
              && resource.data.role == "member"
         )

with:

         (
              isGroupModerator(groupId)
              && resource.data.role == "member"
         )

This gives Aides the same limited student-removal moderation authority as
group moderators, while owner/admin hierarchy remains intact.

NOTE:
The assignment rule already uses classTeacher(groupId), so after step 1
Aides are automatically allowed to create/update/delete assignments.
